at if Bob is round, it must also be blue.\n\nIf something is not blue and furry, then it is not smart.\n\nIf something is not blue and furry, it is not smart.\n\nIf Charlie is not nice or Charlie is not big, then Charlie is not quiet.\n\nFrom the information, we know that Charlie is not nice.\nFrom the information, we know that all nice things are not big.\nFrom the information, we know that all big things are not furry.\nFrom the information, we know that all furry things are not blue.\n\nTherefore, since Charlie is not nice and not big, and all nice and big things are not furry, and all furry things are not blue, it follows that Charlie must not be blue.\n\nThus, the statement "Charlie is blue" is false based on the given information.\n\n<answer>\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
