messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nAnne is nice. Anne is white. Anne is young. Dave is cold. Dave is nice. Dave is smart. Erin is cold. Erin is not kind. Erin is not nice. Erin is smart. Erin is young. Fiona is kind. Smart people are white. Kind, cold people are smart. Kind people are big. If Fiona is cold and Fiona is big then Fiona is nice. If someone is nice and big then they are cold. If someone is young and white then they are cold. If Anne is nice then Anne is cold. Big, young people are nice. Big people are young.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or unknown? Fiona is not big.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Unknown', '<think>.\nTo determine whether the statement "Fiona is not big" is true, false, or unknown based on the given context, we need to analyze the information provided step by step.\n\n1.**Identify relevant information about Fiona:**.\n   - Fiona is kind.\n   - Kind, cold people are smart.\n   - Kind people are big.\n   - If Fiona is cold and Fiona is big, then Fiona is nice.\n   - If someone is nice and big, then they are cold.\n   - If someone is young and white, then they are cold.\n   - If Anne is nice, then Anne is cold.\n   - Big, young people are nice.\n   - Big people are young.\n\n2.**Analyze the relationships between attributes:**.\n   - From "Kind, cold people are smart," we know that Fiona being kind implies she is cold.\n   - From "Kind people are big," we know that Fiona being kind implies she is big.\n   - From "If Fiona is cold and Fiona is big, then Fiona is nice," we know that if Fiona is both cold and big, she must be nice.\n   - From "If someone is nice and big, then they are cold," we know that if Fiona is nice and big, she must be cold.\n   - From "If someone is young and white, then they are cold," we know that if Fiona is young and white, she must be cold.\n   - From "If Anne is nice, then Anne is cold," we know that if Anne is nice, she must be cold.\n   - From "Big, young people are nice," we know that if Fiona is big and young, she must be nice.\n   - From "Big people are young," we know that if Fiona is big, she must be young.\n\nThe statement "Fiona is not big" is true.\nTherefore, Fiona is not big.\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
