ed, we need to check if it is smart.\n   - According to the rule "If something is smart and not red then it is not green," we need to see if Charlie is green.\n   - From the context, we know that Charlie is not blue.\n   - Since Charlie is not blue, it is green.\n\n5.**Conclusion:**.\n   - Since Charlie is not red and green, it satisfies the condition "If something is smart and not red then it is not green.".\n   - Therefore, Charlie is not smart.\n\n<answer>\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
